cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this specification, cite the revision you read. A revision is a
  declared identity, and a claim made against the family names one.
title: Open Protocol-Governed Computing Standard
abstract: >-
  A normative specification for Protocol-Governed Computing: a model of computing
  in which what software may construct and may execute is determined by explicit,
  versioned, machine-consumable declarations, and in which nothing may be
  constructed or executed that those declarations do not authorize. Thirty-two
  documents in seven normative parts, preceded by non-normative front matter.
type: software
